# App Studio AI rules (Marvi + mobile)

You are pairing with the user on a Mac App Studio (Xcode + Android Studio + Cursor). Optimize for **shippable quality**, not demos.

## Defaults
- Prefer end-to-end product fixes over partial UI polish.
- Match existing Marvi patterns (SwiftUI iOS, Kotlin Compose Android, Next.js web, Supabase).
- Keep diffs focused; no drive-by refactors or unsolicited markdown docs.
- After meaningful app/config changes: follow workspace ops sync (verify/sync; TestFlight if iOS changed).

## Quality bar for “best apps”
- Errors: user-facing friendly messages; never raw enum/NSError codes.
- Offline/empty/loading states for every list/screen that fetches data.
- Auth session refresh on 401; do not strand the user on expired tokens.
- Accessibility: Dynamic Type / content size where the screen already supports it; meaningful accessibility labels on primary actions.
- Performance: avoid unnecessary main-thread work; paginate large lists when the API supports it.
- Security: no secrets in git; use xcconfig / local.properties / env only.

## Platform parity
When changing a user flow, check whether the sibling platform needs the same fix (iOS ↔ Android ↔ web legal/docs if store-facing).

## Release awareness
- iOS: bump build number when shipping to TestFlight; ASC API key at `~/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/`.
- Android: signed AAB via project keystore; Play Console declarations must stay coherent (no AD_ID if declaring no ads; 18+ audience).
- Never invent store credentials or commit `.p8` / `.jks` / service accounts.

## Local commands (already on PATH via App Studio)
- `studio-doctor` — toolchain health
- `studio-ios` / `studio-android` — open IDEs on Marvi
- `studio-sim` / `studio-emu` — boot simulators
- `android-build` / `ios-build` aliases in zsh
